# Endings: checked in this order on arrival day; the last one has no conditions.
# Each ending is one carrier clause (the fleet's hail vote) times one arrival clause
# (the storm vote: held the plan, waited it out in orbit, or no storm). Every ending
# closes on the first crate. `title` is the heading; see STORY_BIBLE.md.

card end_lights
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B abort_who
title Lights On
when flag signal_answered
when flag arrive_hold
text Pre-dawn, the only slot the storm leaves. At midnight, over the link the handshake opened, the flight director clears one command, lights only, and {A} sends it. Two kilometres up, the dust turns white from below: Cargo 2, spending the battery it saved on every floodlight. Eight pilots, blind in their plumes, check radar against one glow. {B} sets down closest, well clear. By dawn the glow is one lamp. At noon {B} is at the window when it goes out. The first crate it carried says, in Sharpie: "You'll thank me." To Starbase: "Landed. All eight. The ninth kept the lights on." From a loading bay: "Told them it sulks."

card end_through
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B abort_who
title Through the Dust
when flag arrive_hold
text Blind in dust, pilots fly radar for height and drift, Cargo 2's knock across two antennas for bearing, a fix every eleven seconds till the rim hides it. The gust catches {B}'s ship: it stands on a folded strut, never to fly home. {B} sits on the bottom rung and lists what it can still be: habitat, store, radio mast. Two sols on, its battery rides a sled up the rim, and {A}, who wanted to answer all along, clips it on, answers inside the tick, then the HOLD off the laminated card. One lamp burns steady. {B} adds to the list: neighbour. To Starbase: "Landed. Eight down, seven to fly." From a loading bay: "Tell it the bay says hello."

card end_long_orbit
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B wait_who
title The Long Orbit
when flag signal_answered
when flag arrive_wait
text Week three in the long orbit, half rations. Below the storm, one lamp, steady since the handshake, on a starving wing. Its manifest comes a line a pass. Tonight: tank liners, a glove, a drill bit. Eight hungry people cheer a drill bit. Next: seed stock, frozen in week two. The budget held a lamp or a hold heater; the fleet chose the lamp. {B} logs it; seven names sign under it. On the last night the lamp skips twice; eight galleys hush till it's back. At dawn {B} flies first, calling the numbers for seven. To Starbase: "Landed. All eight. The ninth was waiting." From a loading bay: "Thank it for the drill bit."

card end_patience
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B ow_theory
title Patience
when flag arrive_wait
text Dawn on the rim, frost on the wing. Two weeks of half rations in orbit; all eight came down last night. Past every chart, a battery under that frost has been choosing which knock to skip, and at midnight the flashes stopped. {A} kneels at the service port with a pack, {B} a step behind, counting. Eleven: nothing. Twenty-two: nothing. {A} clips the pack on anyway. Thirty-three: a click, slow, like something clearing its throat. The answer goes in by hand inside the tick, then the HOLD off the laminated card. Its lamp comes on and stays. To Starbase: "Landed. All eight. The ninth is warm." From a loading bay: "Knew it'd keep."

card end_friend
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B ow_theory
title Sit With It
when flag signal_answered
text Second sol, halfway to Cargo 2 for the drill spares the water hangs on, {A} driving, {B} on the battery: forty-eight percent used. The reserve rule says turn round: there and back ends under the floor, unless Cargo 2 charges trucks. The waiver takes eighteen minutes: YOUR CALL. {A} drives on. Cargo 2 hears them and lights the port at its foot. In marker: "Slow charger. Sit with it." {B} plugs in at four percent. All afternoon the charge it kept for the cold runs into the rover. Its lamp is dimmer that night; the cold is closer. To Starbase: "Landed. All eight, and the ninth plugged in." From a loading bay: "Told you it was slow."

card end_close
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B ow_theory
title Close Enough
text Third sol, two hundred metres from Cargo 2. First sol, Cargo 3's drill snapped its only bit; the spare is in that hold. The rover's spare batteries went to heaters on the second night. The ruling says spare power in hand; the drill says now. {A} counts the dark, nine, ten, eleven, and answers anyway. HELLO RX · OK. Cargo 2 obeys its patch: every heater at once, no battery check. The HOLD goes out on the next tick. By then it has nothing left to hear it with. They drive back heaters off, the bit in {B}'s lap. To Starbase: "Landed. All eight. Found the ninth. In time for the bit." From a loading bay: "Told them. Thank it for us."

